§2. Third-party / ported components — retained under their original licenses
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following components are included from upstream projects and remain under
their original (MIT) licenses. Their original copyright notices and permission
terms are preserved, and any attribution requirements must continue to be
honored when these components are used. The provisions of §1 do NOT apply to
the components listed here.

(a) `skills/research/arxiv/` — ported from NousResearch/hermes-agent (MIT).
    The `SKILL.md` and the bundled `scripts/search_arxiv.py` retain the MIT
    License of the upstream project. The skill's frontmatter and the script
    header record the upstream origin.

(b) Skills obtained at runtime via `birkin skills sync` and stored under
    `~/.birkin/skills/mirrors/` retain their upstream licenses (typically MIT
    for hermes-agent skills). These are obtained by the user from the upstream
    source at runtime; birkin does not redistribute them in its source tree or
    distribution artifacts.

See `NOTICE` for the attribution summary.
